From ad7fca5b63d37aad091256f735a8eeaf19414e47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:54:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): count shadow history before capping and disable
 remote card mutations [daveey]

Address independent review of PR #3774: filter live collisions before the final done window and count all matching replica done rows; retain batched home metadata with materialized rows; don't invalidate on shm read marks. Keep live board/show readable if replica queries fail. Apply explicit CLI sorting across the combined row list without writing either DB. Disable drag, bulk selection, file drops and card context mutations for read-only replicas.

Proof: 35 focused CLI/API tests pass, including capped history, off-payload collision, unknown owner, unreadable replica, all nine canonical sorts, unchanged replica bytes, and dispatcher non-claim. Source-only revert to reviewed head produces 10 failing tests. Desktop remote-card/API tests: 22 passed; source-only revert fails. Desktop tsc passes with 3GB heap. Full scripts/check: 21 checks pass.
